+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## Intent
+
+Build a TodoMVC app per `assets/app-spec.md`, using `assets/app-template.index.html` as base markup.
+Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. Persisted to localStorage (key `todos-[framework]`).
+Routing via hashchange on `#/` (all), `#/active`, `#/completed`.
+
+## Specs authored
+
+- `features/todo-core.feature` — add, toggle, delete, mark-all, clear-completed, UI visibility rules
+- `features/todo-editing.feature` — double-click edit, save/cancel, trim/empty-destroy
+- `features/todo-routing.feature` — all/active/completed filters, hash routing, counter, main/footer visibility
+- `features/todo-persistence.feature` — localStorage CRUD, reload survival
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Dependency `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` added to `package.json` per spec requirement.
+- No external router dependency (Director). Happy-dom world.js provides click-intercepted hashchange, so app uses native `hashchange`.
+- Single test tier: happy-dom (cheapest sufficient for DOM observation).
+- Scenarios written at the user-behaviour level, suitable for QM step definition binding.
+
+## Watchbill
+
+6 watches: QV1 (Core CRUD), QV2 (Bulk Ops), QV3 (Editing), QV4 (Filtering/Routing), QV5 (Counter/Visibility), QV6 (Persistence). See `watchbill.json`.
+
+## Next
+
+Dispatch QM to write step definitions and implement step bindings against the app. Deck is clean — no uncommitted production code.
\ No newline at end of file
