+Feature: Todo Filtering and Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And the following todos exist:
+      | title       |
+      | Buy milk    |
+      | Walk dog    |
+      | Do laundry  |
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Rule: All filter
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos by default
+    When the app loads
+    Then all 3 todos are visible
+
+  Scenario: All filter link is selected by default
+    Then the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Selecting All filter shows all todos
+    When I click the "All" filter link
+    Then all 3 todos are visible
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then 2 todos are visible
+    And the visible todos are "Walk dog" and "Do laundry"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter link gets selected class
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the "All" filter link does not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Todo hidden when toggled in Active filter
+    Given I am viewing the "Active" filter
+    When I click the toggle for "Walk dog"
+    Then the todo "Walk dog" is removed from the visible list
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When I click the "Completed" filter link
+    Then 1 todo is visible
+    And the visible todos are "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter link gets selected class
+    When I click the "Completed" filter link
+    Then the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the "All" filter link does not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Todo shown when toggled in Completed filter
+    Given I am viewing the "Completed" filter
+    When I click the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed from the visible list
+
+  Rule: Routing
+
+  Scenario: Hash route #/ shows all
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then all 3 todos are visible
